## aym-skills (paste into ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md)

For any actionable work (building, fixing, planning, reviewing, shipping, pausing or resuming), start with the `work-my-way` skill from the aym-skills plugin. It picks the phase and the skill. A named skill (for example `/aym-skills:check-this`) can be used directly. Simple factual questions don't need it.

Stop after every phase (clarify, plan, build, check, ship) and end it with the aym-skills stop card:
✔ <Phase> done — <result>
Saved: <file paths, or "nothing saved">
Needs from you: <what the user must do now, or "nothing">
Next: <phase> (<skill>). Say "go", or tell me what to change.
